14501	{"artifactId":"LLD-2f27754d4ad00b8e-s9","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-2f27754d4ad00b8e-s9-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:04:30.330Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design covers ac27, ac28 and ac29 (DEF revision 2) and builds no non-goal; the dropped second half of ac29 (older-clone notice) is not built.","evidence":"DEF.md:254-256: ac27 conversion in one commit with Epic/Story/Task heads and a migrated log; ac28 repeat/preview/verify through the delivery reader; ac29 'new tools ... refuse with a clear message ... builds from before this model are not expected to work'. LLD §2.1-2.9, §3.15 and §7 Backward compat cover each; no notice file or compatibility reader is designed. 'One commit' is met by step 11 (the user commits), with runConversion leaving the tree for one commit. [files: docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"runConversion 'verify' mode on its own (after apply has run and the legacy stamps are gone) can build a before-snapshot 'from the converted heads' migrated entries'.","evidence":"§2.6 verifyConversion takes `before: DeliverySnapshot`, which §2.2 says only legacyDeliveryView builds, from RawHead legacy stamps. After apply those stamps are stripped (§3.6/§3.7), so legacyDeliveryView has nothing to read. §2.7 claims verify mode 'recomputes the before-snapshot from the converted heads' migrated entries', but no function, mapping or test (convert-verify.test.ts covers only apply-then-verify) designs that path. ac28's verification is therefore designed only inside apply. [files: docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/S009/LLD.md]","action":"Add a contract (e.g. snapshotFromMigratedEntries) that rebuilds the DeliverySnapshot from the migrated-<id>-approve/-reject/-review/-mark-stale entries, or state that verify mode is only available inside apply. Add a test for a standalone verify run.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A content write through ArtifactStore on a head with meta.lifecycle moves meta.revision and returns the head to draft when the content hash changes, so the store cannot be the conversion's write path.","evidence":"src/workflow/storage.ts:252-257 prepareArtifactWrite: `if (reconciled.contentChanged) { meta['revision'] = readRevision(prior) + 1; ...}`; src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts:164-168 reconcileLifecycle returns `status: 'draft'` on a content change. [files: src/workflow/storage.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The delivery reader derives approval only from the legacy stamps and reads no meta.lifecycle.","evidence":"grep for 'lifecycle' under src/workflow/delivery finds no match. src/workflow/delivery/load.ts:50-57 approvalOf reads fields['approvedAt'] / rejectedAt / status; gate.ts:96-98 maps record.approval. [files: src/workflow/delivery/load.ts, src/workflow/delivery/gate.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"findings.ts stamps meta.review with a meta-only write and records nothing on the lifecycle; tracker-auto readReview (377-381) reads meta.review raw.","evidence":"src/daemon/steps/review-step/phases/findings.ts:91 `writeArtifact(state.jsonPath, { ...artifact, meta: { ...artifact.meta, review: report } }, 'meta-only')`. There is no lifecycle call in the file. src/workflow/tracker-auto.ts:378-382 returns `meta?.review` from the raw JSON. [files: src/daemon/steps/review-step/phases/findings.ts, src/workflow/tracker-auto.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.4","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"convertLegacyFeedback today builds actor 'unknown:<author>', maps only suggestion vs comment, and reports a foreign target.file as unmapped.","evidence":"src/workflow/artifact-core/feedback-convert.ts:51-53 pushes target.file to unmapped; :58 `actor: { id: `unknown:${entry.author}`, kind: 'person', properties: {} }`; :61 `kind: entry.kind === 'suggestion' ? 'suggestion' : 'comment'`. The §2.10 changes are real changes to the current code. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/feedback-convert.ts]","action":"Note: the current code already maps anchor.sectionSlug to anchor.section (:40). Putting a foreign target.file in anchor.section would overwrite a sectionSlug. State which value wins.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"RepoSchemaGate.require(repo, atLeast) and the RepoSchema { version, convertedAt } shape already exist (sc8), and this Story only adds the writer.","evidence":"src/workflow/artifact-core/repo-schema.ts:21-47 has read() and require() with the stated return union; types.ts:184-187 has RepoSchema { version; convertedAt? }. There is no writer today. The current message names 'the s9 conversion', not repo.convert, so §2.9's message text is a small change. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/repo-schema.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/types.ts]","action":"Change the require() message to name repo.convert, as §2.9 states.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Reused shapes exist: Review.report is a Reference that supports relation 'reviews'; ChangeLogEntry.outcome carries data; History.appendLog and ArtifactStore.exclusive exist.","evidence":"types.ts:28-34 Reference.relation includes 'reviews'; :121-129 Review.report?: Reference; :65 outcome { result; summary; data?: unknown }; history.ts:100 appendLog; store.exclusive is used at task-set.ts:338 and comment-sync.ts:153. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/types.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/history.ts]","action":"history.ts:56 validateLogEntry requires outcome.result and outcome.summary as text. The migrated and review entries must set both, not only outcome.data.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.3","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"TaskSets.createFromPlan already moves the Plan's Task tracker record onto each Task head and is repeatable, so the conversion needs no Task-record writer.","evidence":"src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts:141-146 doc: 'A Task record found on the plan is moved onto its head's binding. A repeat for the same plan revision writes nothing'. :204 ensureTask calls this.moveRecord(p, row, id); :152-153 returns early when the TASKS head exists. [files: src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The inventory of meta.review / reviewResolutions readers and writers in §3.4, §3.7 and §3.9 is complete.","evidence":"grep for meta.review / ['review'] / reviewResolutions outside tests finds 19 files. All production readers and writers are listed (gates, resolve, party, tracker-auto, delivery gate/currency/types, artifact-content, workflow-rpc, mcp/server, cli/services/workflow, findings, verdicts, run-artifact, artifact-write-inventory). decode.ts:70 reads lifecycle.review, not the stamp. canonical.ts:92 only deletes a key. code-review/gate.ts mentions it in a comment. [files: src/workflow/gates.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/decode.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The legacy approval stamps to retire are approvedAt, rejectedAt, rejectReason, reviewOverride, staleAckedAt, review and reviewResolutions; deleting the gates' stamp writing (STAMP_KEYS) leaves nothing else unaccounted for.","evidence":"src/workflow/gates.ts:876 `const STAMP_KEYS = ['approvedAt', 'rejectedAt', 'rejectReason', 'rangeBase', 'reviewOverride']`. gates.ts:680-687 stamps meta.rangeBase at approval. src/workflow/runners/build/range-base.ts:296-302 reads `meta.rangeBase` to resolve a Story's build range, and completion-record.ts:80 uses it. The LLD lists range-base.ts in §3.6 ('move to LifecycleService and delete the stamp') but never names rangeBase. It is not in the lifecycle fields (§3.3), the strip list, the post-apply legacy-field sweep or the contract source check. The lifecycle has no field for it. Building this as written either strips rangeBase and breaks build-range resolution for approved Stories, or leaves it as an undeclared legacy field. [files: src/workflow/gates.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/range-base.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/completion-record.ts]","action":"State where meta.rangeBase lives after conversion: kept as a non-lifecycle meta field, moved to the approve change-log entry, or recomputed. Add it to the strip, keep and contract-test lists accordingly.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Appending a revision-bearing migrated-<id> entry with the head's kept revision number and the converted content hash, timestamped with the conversion clock, makes checkIntegrity pass against heads that already have an s4 log.","evidence":"lifecycle.ts:133-142 checkIntegrity compares the head with the last entry that carries a revision (`[...log].reverse().find(e => e.revision !== undefined)`) by number and hash. history.ts:122-124 says the reader orders entries by timestamp, then id, so the conversion-clock entry is last. Revision-less stamp entries with older original times do not stand in for it. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/history.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The migration write is conversion-owned and leaves the sc2 ArtifactStore contract unchanged, using only existing primitives (store.exclusive, writeAtomic).","evidence":"src/workflow/storage.ts:81 exports writeAtomic(absPath, content). store.exclusive is an existing method used by task-set.ts:338 and feedback-service.ts:62. §3.5 and §4 sc2 add no method to the store. Alternative a2 (an sc2 amendment) is rejected. artifactOfUnit (comment-sync.ts:81) is not among s8's private items. [files: src/workflow/storage.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/store.ts, src/workflow/tracker/comment-sync.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Apply is crash-safe and rerunnable after every rule: 'a crash injected after each step of writeMigratedHead and each rule, then a rerun, gives the same result as an uninterrupted run', given the stated rule order (migrate every head, then convert body.feedback, ..., strip the legacy fields last).","evidence":"§3.5 and §3.10 say the migration write strips body.feedback and the legacy fields. §2.3 and §7 step 7 run 'migrate every head' before 'convert body.feedback'. The planner reads only the stored files (§2.1). A crash after a head is replaced and before its feedback is converted leaves a head with no body.feedback and no Feedback lines, so the rerun has nothing to convert and the feedback is lost from the working tree; only git still has it. The same order also conflicts with 'strip the legacy fields' as the last rule: if stripping happens later, the contentHash written by writeMigratedHead no longer matches the head and checkHeadIntegrity (lifecycle.ts:122-124) fails. history.ts:106-110 appendFeedback is a separate append, not part of the head write. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/history.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts, docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/S009/LLD.md]","action":"Order convert-body.feedback (append the Feedback lines with their deterministic ids) before the migration write of the same head, and make the migration write the single step that strips body.feedback and the legacy fields. Then contentHash is computed once over the final content, and a rerun always finds either the raw entries or the appended lines. Drop or redefine the trailing 'strip the legacy fields' rule.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each acceptance criterion (ac27, ac28, ac29) maps to at least one named test that exercises it.","evidence":"The §6 acceptance mapping gives ac27 → convert-apply, convert-lifecycle-backfill, convert-feedback, convert-ids, convert-tasks, convert-story-history; ac28 → convert-preview, convert-repeat (including the crash-and-rerun case), convert-verify; ac29 → repo-schema-entry-points, convert-marker. These match DEF.md:254-256. The crash-and-rerun test in convert-repeat would expose the rule-order defect reported under error-paths. [files: docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md]","action":"Add a test for standalone verify mode and a rangeBase keep/strip test once those are designed.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":1,"med":2,"low":12,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-22T06:04:30.330Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
